  "estimatedLength": "25 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Describe Mars's apparent retrograde path against background stars, including normal eastward drift, temporary westward reversal, and return to eastward motion.",
    "Explain apparent retrograde motion in the heliocentric model as a consequence of Earth overtaking a slower outer planet.",
    "Contrast geocentric epicycle-based and heliocentric explanations of retrograde motion, and explain why the heliocentric model is more parsimonious.",
    "Predict when retrograde motion will occur for an outer planet based on the relative orbital positions of Earth and that planet.",
    "Compare retrograde loops for Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn, and explain why more distant planets show smaller apparent loops."
  ],
